+## Native Firedancer Intel configuration stage
+
+The native `firedancer configure init iavf` stage loads `vfio-pci`, creates or reuses a VF, and replaces PF ntuple rules with Firedancer UDP drop rules. It requires root and, when loading the module, `CAP_SYS_MODULE`. `check iavf` verifies the configured state without changes. `fini iavf` clears PF rules and removes VF 0 when exactly one VF exists; it retains multiple VFs and does not unload the module or restore previous filters. See [initialization](../guide/initializing.md#iavf). This backport does not add the stage to Frankendancer `fdctl`.
